// @@@ For all valid indices i, if the index i is greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the list, then for all indices j such that index<j and j<old(this.size()-1), the element at index j in the list is either null or equal to the previous element in the list.

--------------------
// @@@ For every index 'i' that is greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the list, the property holds that for all indices 'j' such that 'index<j' and 'j<old(this.size()-1)', if the element at index 'j' is null and the element at index 'j+1' is also null, then the elements at indices 'j' and 'j+1' are equal. Otherwise, the elements at indices 'j' and 'j+1' can be different.

--------------------
// @@@ For every index 'i' that is greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the list, the value at index 'j' is equal to the value at index 'j+1' if 'j' is less than 'i' and 'j' is less than the old size of the list minus 1.

